{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":250351,"duration_api_ms":249550,"num_turns":37,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d8e2fabe-6ed3-4421-a627-81b5c992383a","total_cost_usd":1.4105975,"usage":{"input_tokens":25,"cache_creation_input_tokens":79020,"cache_read_input_tokens":1427295,"output_tokens":8118,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":79020,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":25,"outputTokens":8118,"cacheReadInputTokens":1427295,"cacheCreationInputTokens":79020,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.4105975,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Reviewed the concentration helper implementation (water.rs, state.rs, geometry.rs, snapshot.rs, all system files, and concentration_helpers.rs tests). The core implementation is correct: the `concentration()` function properly guards against zero/NaN volume, all system files are migrated from ad-hoc division to canonical helpers, and substrate displacement is properly subtracted from gross volume. Tests pass. No functional bugs found. I identified five issues: a latent correctness fragility in `seeded_example()`, missing test coverage for several helpers, a missing DON helper, an inline KH formula that should be a helper, and repeated volume recomputation in hot paths.","amendments":[{"body":"`TankState::seeded_example()` (state.rs:105-133) replaces `substrate_layers` after `new()` already computed water totals based on the default substrate depth. The total depth happens to match (default 3.0 cm = seeded_example 2.0+1.0 cm), but this is coincidental. If either default changes, dissolved-mass totals will be wrong for the new volume, silently producing incorrect concentrations. Add a `rescale_totals_for_volume()` call or rebuild `WaterState` after setting the new substrate layers, mirroring what `apply_startup_overrides` already does.","rationale":"This is a latent correctness bug that will silently produce wrong concentrations if substrate defaults diverge. The fix pattern already exists in apply_startup_overrides (lib.rs:597-601)."},{"body":"The proptest and unit tests in concentration_helpers.rs only cover 8 of 13 helpers. `calcium_mg_per_l()`, `magnesium_mg_per_l()`, `gh_d()`, `tds_mg_per_l()`, and `conductivity_us_cm()` are missing from both the known-value unit test (`canonical_helpers_use_net_water_volume`) and the non-negativity property test. The acceptance criteria requires 'unit tests for every helper method' and 'helpers never return negative values (property test)'. Add assertions for all five missing helpers in both the unit test and the proptest.","rationale":"Acceptance criteria explicitly requires every helper to have both known-value unit tests and property tests for non-negativity. Five helpers are uncovered."},{"body":"Add a `don_mg_n_per_l()` (dissolved organic nitrogen) concentration helper to WaterState and TankState. The field `dissolved_organic_nitrogen_mg_n_total` exists and is actively used in nitrogen_cycle.rs (lines 77, 99-104) and water_change.rs, but has no canonical concentration accessor. The acceptance criteria says 'helper coverage is enough to support nitrogen... refactors', and tanksim-6e5.2.3 (normalize nitrogen-cycle kinetics to concentration-based terms) is a direct dependent that will need DON concentration.","rationale":"DON is a nitrogen pool actively used in the nitrogen cycle. Omitting it forces the next bead (tanksim-6e5.2.3) to derive DON concentration ad-hoc, which is exactly the pattern these helpers are meant to eliminate."},{"body":"Add a `kh_d()` helper to WaterState/TankState, analogous to the existing `gh_d()`. Currently snapshot.rs:73 computes KH inline as `(state.alkalinity_meq_per_l() * 50.0) / 17.848`. This is the same kind of ad-hoc re-derivation the helpers are designed to prevent, and it creates an asymmetry where GH has a canonical helper but KH does not.","rationale":"KH (carbonate hardness) is a standard aquarium parameter that will be needed by the carbonate solver (tanksim-6e5.4.2). Leaving it inline while GH has a helper is inconsistent with the stated design goal of 'one canonical place'."},{"body":"Each TankState concentration helper (tan_mg_n_per_l, nitrite_mg_n_per_l, etc.) independently calls `self.water_volume_l()`, which iterates `substrate_layers` to sum depths each time. In `TankSnapshot::from_state()` (snapshot.rs:64-75), this recomputes the substrate sum and volume ~13 times. Consider either (a) caching substrate_depth_cm/water_volume_l on TankState when substrate_layers changes, or (b) having a `ConcentrationView` struct that computes volume once and provides all accessors. The current approach is O(helpers × layers) per snapshot.","rationale":"Snapshot creation runs every simulation tick. With the current 13 helpers each recomputing volume via substrate iteration, this is measurably wasteful. The bead description itself suggests 'a ConcentrationView struct' as an option."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"8dd6381e-fd75-4c56-82d9-44c578aa23e1"}
